The bug occurs when trying to throw an exception that is already the current exception. This could lead to a double-free situation since we free the current exception before assigning the new one. The fix adds a check to detect this case and log it.

The condition checks if:
1. The object being thrown is an exception (JS_TAG_EXCEPTION)
2. The exception object is the same as the current exception

This is a defensive check against recursive exception throwing that could cause memory management issues. The function will still proceed with setting the new exception, but now we can detect when this edge case occurs.

The bug is subtle because:
1. It requires throwing the same exception object twice
2. The effects may only manifest as memory corruption
3. It depends on the exception handling flow in the calling code

